                <pb facs="1032" n="918" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg918"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.001 Montero, Juan/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-27T17:00:00-05:00">November 27, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>56. Reference Embassy’s despatch No. 1013, November 5, 1931. At the time of the
                    inauguration of President Montero, you may extend to <pb facs="1033" n="919"
                        xml:id="pg919"/> him the cordial congratulations of the President and the
                    assurances of his best wishes for the success of Señor Montero’s
                    administration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
